# write then slurp roundtrip: write "hello tinct" to target/, read it back
# % is used as an intermediate expression in the second document to force
# materialization of the write side-effect before the slurp runs.
[write [narrow %cwd "target"] "tinct-test-write-slurp.txt" "hello tinct"]
---
%
[slurp [open [narrow %cwd "target"] "tinct-test-write-slurp.txt" Readable]]
=== out
String("hello tinct")
